(property "Description" "Concrete BOM candidate, leaded bead NTC:10k at25C +/-1%, B25/50=3950K +/-1%. Use maker R/T table, not a generic beta curve outside its defined range. | design | Maker revA2.0 states operating-20 to120C, bead diameter up to2.2mm, body length4mm and nominal lead pitch2.0mm. Confirm purchased lead dimensions against the drawing; one printed wire-tolerance value appears malformed, so do not infer it.; Mount the panel sensor on the rear heat spreader near the panel hot spot; mount the case sensor on the inner frame away from direct converter heat. Electrically insulate and strain-relieve the leads, solder at least6mm from the bead per maker instruction. Attachment thickness and lag require installed calibration.; Reference-fed10k divider is ratiometric toADC_VREF. At25C nominal sensor power is0.225mW; with maker dissipation coefficient>=2mW/C the still-air self-heating estimate is<=0.113C. This is a model, not a measured mounted offset.; Use maker table R60C=2.4734k and R68C=1.8623k for thermal acceptance points. Verify sensor open/short/stale data drives fail-safe full cooling. Calibrate actual installed temperature at25/60/68C." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
